# Training Compound on a later turn: it did not enter this turn, and the only other land Bot1 controls, Rockfall Vale, is not basic
# (CR 205.4a), so its second ability is refused for red and for green; the first ability, {T}: Add {C}, is the positive control and
# works. (The Vale enters tapped, fewer than two other lands.) Bot2 plays an Island: a basic land, but not one Bot1 controls.

[Bot1 Deck]
Training Compound
Rockfall Vale
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Training Compound.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Rockfall Vale.Play
! Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Activate(Ability: {R} or {G}; Color: Red)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Activate(Ability: {R} or {G}; Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Activate(Ability: Add {C}.)

[Expect]
Bot1.Mana = {C}
Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Tapped = true
